monkey brought online 2026-08-03; only ecosim@monkey may dispatch.

Self-dev has moved off mandark (realisateur/MONKEY.md). Until monkey has been
watched through several real cycles, this file makes "one dispatcher" a
MECHANICAL fact rather than a property of three conf files that all happen to
agree today: bin/freeze-check.sh refuses dispatch at exit 1 for anything not
named below, on every host, regardless of what any rotation says.

The host-scoped form is used deliberately. A bare `EXEMPT: ecosim` would
unfreeze ecosim everywhere, including on mandark where its row still exists in
_paced.conf at enabled=0 -- and a single edit there would then arm a second
host silently. Naming the host means the exemption cannot travel.

EXEMPT: ecosim@monkey
